    "q-346397": {
      "dom_id": "step-q346397",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}3{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x=$  \n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "If we let $u=4x,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u=\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nComputing our limits of integration, we get the following:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\operatorname{ln}⁡3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $4\\operatorname{ln}⁡3$ |\n\nThen, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}3{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{0}^{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{e}^{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({3}^{4})}{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot {e}^{u}\\,{|}_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({3}^{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}({e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({3}^{4})}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}({3}^{4}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}(81-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot 80 \\\\  & =60\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
