    "q-73668": {
      "dom_id": "step-q73668",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "Calculate the integral $\\int 8\\cdot {2}^{4x+6}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's introduce the new variable $u=4x+6.$ Differentiating gives \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=4\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 8\\cdot {2}^{4x+6}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2\\cdot {2}^{4x+6}\\cdot 4\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int {2}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot {2}^{u}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot {2}^{4x+6}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{2}^{4x+7}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
